	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Dustwallow Marsh is a drowned country of black water, reed and mist on the eastern coast of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, south of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}. Its roads sink into mud, its trees rot where they stand, and crocolisks lie in every pool. At its eastern edge, on an island in the bay, stands the white city of {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}, a refuge for the humans who crossed the sea after the fall of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. In the west, the ogres of the Stonemaul clan crowd into a village of huts among the reeds. And in the far south, where the fen turns to scorched rock, black dragons nest in the {link:wyrmbog}Wyrmbog{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records who first named the marsh, or what peoples walked its shores before the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. What is told is that {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} led the survivors of the northern kingdoms across the sea to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. After the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, she chose an island off the coast of this swamp for their new home and raised {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} upon it. There she kept the peace she had made with {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}. When her father, Admiral {link:daelin-proudmoore}Daelin Proudmoore{/link}, came with his fleet to destroy the orcs, the war reached the gates of Theramore, and the admiral died before its walls. His daughter did not stand with him.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} stands, but the marsh around it does not belong to it. Its soldiers hold a few towers, but they have lost control of the roads. Some of the marines who came with the Proudmoore fleet have deserted rather than serve a lady who made peace with orcs. {link:horde}Horde{/link} spies watch the city from the reeds, and Theramore's own infiltrators watch the Horde. The {link:shady-rest-inn}Shady Rest Inn{/link}, on the western road, has been burned to the ground, and no one knows by whose hand. Even the city's loyalty has cracks: a soldier of Theramore has been found in league with the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link} against the king of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} himself.

In the west, the Stonemaul ogres have fled their old village in the south. {link:rexxar}Rexxar{/link} once made {link:overlord-mok-morokk}Mok'Morokk{/link} their overlord, and Mok'Morokk has grown fat on the office. In the south, the brood of {link:onyxia}Onyxia{/link}, daughter of {link:deathwing}Deathwing{/link}, has claimed the {link:wyrmbog}Wyrmbog{/link}, and her eggs lie scattered across the Dragonmurk.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The people of {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}.{/b} Soldiers, marines of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link}, mages, smiths and traders who crossed the sea with {link:jaina-proudmoore}Lady Proudmoore{/link}.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} Orc agents and {link:ogres}ogres{/link} in {link:brackenwall-village}Brackenwall Village{/link}, watching Theramore and the roads.
• {b}The Stonemaul ogres.{/b} Driven north from their home by the black dragonflight.
• {b}The black dragonflight.{/b} Dragonkin, whelps and drakes of the Firemane and the Searing broods, who serve {link:onyxia}Onyxia{/link} in the south.
• {b}Deserters.{/b} Former soldiers of Theramore who squat in abandoned towers.
• {b}The wild.{/b} Crocolisks, spiders, oozes, muckshell crab-men, {link:murlocs}Mirefin murlocs{/link} and the {link:naga}Strashaz naga{/link} of {link:alcaz-island}Alcaz Island{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Exodus.{/b} {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} led the survivors of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} west across the sea to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}.
• {b}{link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}.{/b} After Hyjal, the refugees built their city on its island, and many of {link:daelin-proudmoore}Daelin{/link}'s marines joined its guard.
• {b}The Admiral's War.{/b} Daelin Proudmoore made war on the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and fell at Theramore.
• {b}The Stonemaul.{/b} {link:rexxar}Rexxar{/link} led the Stonemaul for a time. When he left, {link:overlord-mok-morokk}Mok'Morokk{/link} ruled in his name.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Marsh",
			text = [=[• The {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} guard wears a badge of a gold anchor on white. It is the sign of the city.
• A hermit named {link:tabetha}Tabetha{/link} keeps a cottage deep in the marsh, and mages and warlocks seek her out.
• On an island south of Theramore lives a fisherman who says he has never much enjoyed fishing.]=],
		},
	},
})

